125
00:06:52.572 --> 00:06:55.687
Why load balancers are called L4 or L7.

126
00:06:55.967 --> 00:07:05.183
An L4 load balancer sees TCP or UDP connections (IP + port) and forwards bytes without understanding HTTP.

127
00:07:05.463 --> 00:07:12.865
An L7 load balancer terminates HTTP, so it can route by path or header, retry, and add headers.

128
00:07:13.145 --> 00:07:19.375
