225
00:11:41.975 --> 00:11:44.130
Idle connection TTL in pool.

226
00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:45.071
Where:

227
00:11:45.351 --> 00:11:46.141
Client.

228
00:11:46.421 --> 00:11:47.509
Typical value:

229
00:11:47.789 --> 00:11:50.370
Below the server's or LB's idle timeout.

230
00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:51.333
Why:

231
00:11:51.613 --> 00:11:55.069
Avoid reusing a connection the other side already closed.

232
00:11:56.419 --> 00:11:58.083
Server keep-alive timeout.

233
00:11:58.363 --> 00:11:59.024
Where:

234
00:11:59.304 --> 00:12:01.480
Server (Tomcat or Jetty or Netty).

235
00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:02.848
Typical value:

236
00:12:03.128 --> 00:12:04.813
60 to 75 s.

237
00:12:05.093 --> 00:12:05.776
Why:

238
00:12:06.056 --> 00:12:08.509
Free resources held by idle clients.

239
00:12:08.789 --> 00:12:10.219
LB idle timeout.

240
00:12:10.499 --> 00:12:11.160
Where:

241
00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:12.507
Cloud LB.

242
00:12:12.787 --> 00:12:13.875
Typical value:

243
00:12:14.155 --> 00:12:17.333
60 s default on many LBs; configurable.

244
00:12:17.613 --> 00:12:18.296
Why:

245
00:12:18.576 --> 00:12:21.157
Silently kills idle long-lived connections.

246
00:12:22.507 --> 00:12:23.425
Watch out:

247
00:12:23.705 --> 00:12:25.518
The stale pooled connection bug.

248
00:12:25.798 --> 00:12:36.145
If a client pool keeps idle connections longer than the server or load balancer does, the client sometimes sends a request on a connection the other side has already closed.

249
00:12:36.425 --> 00:12:41.737
The result is an intermittent Connection reset on the first request after a quiet period.

250
00:12:42.017 --> 00:12:50.102
The rule: client idle TTL server keep-alive LB idle timeout, and retry idempotent requests once on a reset.

251
00:12:51.452 --> 00:12:56.593
Head-of-line (HOL) blocking happens when one slow item blocks everything behind it:

252
00:12:57.943 --> 00:12:59.287
