597
00:30:04.133 --> 00:30:05.072
S to R:

598
00:30:05.352 --> 00:30:09.853
XREVRANGE trk:order:42 + - COUNT 1 (current state).

599
00:30:10.133 --> 00:30:11.051
S to App:

600
00:30:11.331 --> 00:30:13.613
200 text or event-stream, id:

601
00:30:13.893 --> 00:30:18.608
1727..-0, event: status, data:

602
00:30:18.888 --> 00:30:19.592
PACKED.

603
00:30:19.872 --> 00:30:24.971
K to RT: order.order.status-changed.v1 42, RIDERASSIGNED.

604
00:30:25.251 --> 00:30:26.317
RT to R:

605
00:30:26.597 --> 00:30:30.032
XADD trk:order:42 status RIDERASSIGNED.

606
00:30:30.312 --> 00:30:31.379
RT to R:

607
00:30:31.659 --> 00:30:35.157
PUBLISH trk:live:42 id, RIDERASSIGNED.

608
00:30:35.437 --> 00:30:38.744
R to S: message on trk:live:42.

609
00:30:39.024 --> 00:30:40.453
S to App: id:

610
00:30:40.733 --> 00:30:45.299
1727..-1, event: status, data:

611
00:30:45.579 --> 00:30:46.667
RIDERASSIGNED.

612
00:30:46.947 --> 00:30:49.720
S to App: : heartbeat (SSE comment line).

613
00:30:53.570 --> 00:30:57.367
Sequence: failure path, network switch mid-delivery and resume.

614
00:30:57.647 --> 00:31:00.442
The sequence diagram walks through it step by step.

615
00:31:00.722 --> 00:31:04.178
App to App: phone moves Wi-Fi, then 4G (new IP).

616
00:31:04.458 --> 00:31:05.610
R to S2:

617
00:31:05.890 --> 00:31:11.010
PUBLISH OUTFORDELIVERY (id 1727..-2).

618
00:31:11.290 --> 00:31:17.029
S2 to App: write fails on next event or heartbeat, then emitter completed, unsubscribe.

619
00:31:17.309 --> 00:31:20.551
App to App: no event or heartbeat for 45 s?

620
00:31:20.831 --> 00:31:21.514
No:

621
00:31:21.794 --> 00:31:24.866
OS reports network change, then reconnect now.

622
00:31:25.146 --> 00:31:27.023
App to NAT: new connection.

623
00:31:27.303 --> 00:31:28.477
NAT to S3:

624
00:31:28.757 --> 00:31:32.255
GET or orders or 42 or events, Last-Event-ID:

625
00:31:32.535 --> 00:31:37.186
1727..-1 (LB picks pod 3).

626
00:31:37.466 --> 00:31:38.575
S3 to R:

627
00:31:38.855 --> 00:31:47.709
XRANGE trk:order:42 (1727..-1 +, then events after the last seen id.

628
00:31:47.989 --> 00:31:49.162
R to S3:

629
00:31:49.442 --> 00:31:53.559
1727..-2 OUTFORDELIVERY.

630
00:31:53.839 --> 00:32:00.239
S3 to App: replay: id 1727..-2 OUTFORDELIVERY.

631
00:32:00.519 --> 00:32:01.629
S3 to R:

632
00:32:01.909 --> 00:32:04.405
SUBSCRIBE trk:live:42.

633
00:32:08.255 --> 00:32:09.001
Note:

634
00:32:09.281 --> 00:32:12.055
What the system guarantees after this failure path.

635
00:32:12.335 --> 00:32:19.225
Every status change is delivered at least once to a client that reconnects within the replay window (3 hours).

636
00:32:19.505 --> 00:32:22.535
Duplicates are removed on the client by event id.

637
00:32:22.815 --> 00:32:30.452
A missed heartbeat is detected within 45 s at most, and an OS-reported network change triggers an immediate reconnect.

638
00:32:30.732 --> 00:32:34.273
No pod stickiness is needed: any pod can serve any order.

639
00:32:35.623 --> 00:32:37.586
